      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/baxterville_mississippi",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town began as a stop on the Gulf and Ship Island Railroad, linking it to lumber and agricultural markets.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/baxterville_mississippi",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "By the early 1900s, Baxterville boasted a turpentine still and two saw mills, fueling local growth.",
